[I] A Virtual File System for looking into archives

[T] AVFS is a system which enables all programs to look inside archived or
[T] compressed files, or access remote files, without recompiling the
[T] programs or changing the kernel. It supports tar, gzip, zip, bzip2, ar
[T] and rar files as well as ftp, http, webdav, rsh and ssh, and can be used
[T] via FUSE or a preloaded library.

[U] https://avf.sourceforge.net/

[A] Avfs Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

